WEBVTT

00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:58.200
What's wrong? Now's your chance.

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:02.080
Old man!

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:09.120
<i>Every man dreams of being</i>
<i>the world's strongest man.</i>

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:13.500
<i>And everyone gives up at some point.</i>

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:16.380
<i>But a small handful of men</i>

00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:19.630
<i>will never give up on their dream.</i>

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:24.680
<i>No matter who or what they face,</i>
<i>even as they become adults.</i>

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:26.980
<i>Baki Hanma.</i>

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:29.480
<i>A boy who desires</i>

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:33.060
<i>to defeat his father, Yujiro Hanma,</i>
<i>the strongest creature on Earth.</i>

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:40.860
<i>The world's strongest death row inmates</i>

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:43.280
<i>suddenly gathered</i>
<i>at Baki's location in Japan.</i>

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:47.370
<i>Baki and the other fighters</i>
<i>met a struggle of life and death.</i>

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:49.660
<i>As a result,</i>

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:52.540
<i>Baki was poisoned in his fight.</i>

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:54.250
<i>On the verge of death,</i>

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:57.510
<i>Baki is rushed to China.</i>

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:07.220
It's been a long time.

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:09.480
Mr. Ogre.

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:12.980
You've grown up, Mohammad Jr.

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:16.070
How is your great father?

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:19.820
<i>Show me.</i>

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:24.070
Your true skill isn't boxing.

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:28.660
What makes you think that?

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:35.590
<i>Watching how you move in the ring,</i>
<i>it's obvious.</i>

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:39.340
An all-compatible fighting technique.

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:42.010
You could call it

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:45.010
the Mohammad Alai Mixed Martial Arts!

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:48.770
But...

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:53.390
unfortunately, it's incomplete.

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:56.770
It's just like you said.

00:03:57.230 --> 00:04:00.570
But after your three-year blank out
because of the draft evasion,

00:04:01.070 --> 00:04:03.280
you lost your footwork.

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:08.490
<i>The style I was searching for myself</i>
<i>was only an illusion.</i>

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:12.330
Your great father
couldn't accomplish his dream.

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:15.920
Are you saying you've completed it?

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:18.420
Yes, that's right.

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:24.180
It seems you doubt me.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:28.350
It can't be described through words.

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:32.930
My father was supposed to finish
the Mohammad Alai Mixed Martial Arts.

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:38.020
It's better if you see
its complete form firsthand.

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:43.950
At least, if it's okay with you.

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:47.240
I'll say this before we begin.

00:04:48.410 --> 00:04:50.950
My fist is as strong as ever.

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:53.540
I won't hold back.

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:56.080
A real fight?

00:04:56.170 --> 00:04:57.710
If that's okay with you.

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:03.420
You're ballsy, kid.

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:13.980
Nice speed.

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:17.100
Your father was a heavyweight,

00:05:17.480 --> 00:05:20.980
but had the speed of
a lightweight or featherweight.

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:24.360
You're at a flyweight's
or a strawweight's speed.

00:05:24.940 --> 00:05:28.070
In other words,
you're faster than your father.

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:32.370
<i>I barely dodged it.</i>

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:36.250
<i>That speed was even faster than a jab.</i>

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:39.420
Your father was great at swaying back.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:41.460
You got it down too.

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:45.510
But what's coming next
is the real problem.

00:05:50.510 --> 00:05:53.510
This is called
the Alai vs. Igari Position.

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:58.600
Surprisingly, after this position
made its appearance,

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:01.770
no one has been able to defeat it.

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:05.780
Now, what will you do?

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:09.360
By the way, the first victim of this move

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:11.280
was your father.

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:15.410
<i>Antonio Igari invented this move</i>
<i>as a last resort.</i>

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:19.330
<i>Your father only yelled,</i>
<i>"Get up and come at me,"</i>

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:21.540
<i>and couldn't even get close.</i>

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:25.760
It looks surmountable at first glance,

00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:29.050
but it's actually pretty troublesome.

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:33.050
Show me what you've got.

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:39.810
Including my father,

00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:45.820
I have no idea why
people struggle with that move.

00:06:46.650 --> 00:06:49.700
Martial arts were originally invented
for the weak

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:52.070
to protect themselves from the strong.

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:56.200
Your strong foe is voluntarily lying down.

00:06:56.740 --> 00:07:00.080
What more would I need to do?

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:04.840
If you're laying down for me,
I just need to leave the room.

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:08.340
What?

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:12.470
I'm glad it all ended peacefully.

00:07:13.390 --> 00:07:14.430
Bye.

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:22.850
You bastard!

00:07:41.750 --> 00:07:43.710
-What is it?
-It's a terrorist attack!

00:07:52.050 --> 00:07:53.630
Raitai?

00:07:54.220 --> 00:07:57.600
It's a martial arts tournament
held in China and Taiwan.

00:07:58.350 --> 00:08:01.230
This is what the tournament arena
is called in Chinese.

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:03.640
And so, Baki...

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:09.650
The Great Raitai Tournament
is held every 100 years.

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:12.820
You will be fighting on the Raitai stage.

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:15.700
Leaving him as he is won't save him!

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:18.660
This is a fight to survive.

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:24.170
But he'll die.
It's crazy for him to fight!

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:27.170
Such an important tournament...

00:08:28.670 --> 00:08:30.170
and I'm in this condition...

00:08:34.220 --> 00:08:35.970
You will want to participate.

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:39.180
I'll want to?

00:08:40.010 --> 00:08:43.180
An unexpected fighter
is participating this year...

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:55.200
Fly me to Hong Kong!

00:08:59.780 --> 00:09:02.450
I apologize for coming like this.

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:07.460
Needless to say, I thank you
for welcoming me at this hour.

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:09.960
Thank you for waiting.

00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:14.970
He's huge!

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:24.060
You look just like your father,
the great boxer, Mohammad Alai.

00:09:25.230 --> 00:09:27.900
The Great Raitai Tournament
held once every century...

00:09:28.060 --> 00:09:31.900
I heard it was possible
for non-Chinese citizens to participate.

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:34.030
It's just as you say.

00:09:35.150 --> 00:09:35.990
However...

00:09:37.150 --> 00:09:38.990
You want me to prove my strength?

00:09:39.870 --> 00:09:41.450
Just as your father did,

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:47.500
through the way he lived his life,
and continued to prove his strength.

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:03.970
Is it really okay to leave
those gloves on?

00:10:04.720 --> 00:10:06.390
It's fine if this is my foe.

00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:10.730
Begin!

00:10:18.650 --> 00:10:19.490
Go ahead.

00:10:20.490 --> 00:10:22.070
Go ahead.

00:10:30.330 --> 00:10:32.210
-What?
-How absurd.

00:10:32.540 --> 00:10:33.380
Go ahead.

00:10:50.730 --> 00:10:52.400
That's right.

00:10:55.730 --> 00:10:57.280
You're better off standing up.

00:11:05.990 --> 00:11:08.910
-He's fast!
-His hits are clearly faster.

00:11:27.770 --> 00:11:31.890
I'm sorry, can I have someone
take off my gloves?

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:39.320
Had the Great Raitai Tournament
happened 30 years ago,

00:11:40.030 --> 00:11:43.950
I would have liked your father
to have participated.

00:11:44.530 --> 00:11:50.410
But it seems like you've perfected
what your father left unfinished.

00:11:52.160 --> 00:11:54.460
The Mohammad Alai Mixed Martial Arts.

00:11:56.210 --> 00:11:57.710
I'm looking forward to it.

00:12:01.550 --> 00:12:02.720
WARRIOR

00:12:19.900 --> 00:12:23.490
Looks like you've prepared well.

00:12:24.070 --> 00:12:26.240
Your fist is ready too.

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:33.500
Will you really...

00:12:38.170 --> 00:12:41.510
fight in the Raitai Tournament tomorrow?

00:12:44.470 --> 00:12:47.760
The Great Raitai Tournament
is held once in a century.

00:12:49.010 --> 00:12:50.770
Do you know

00:12:51.520 --> 00:12:55.770
what this kind of tournament
means to someone like me?

00:13:02.860 --> 00:13:04.900
I will show no mercy.

00:13:09.410 --> 00:13:13.620
Even if my opponent is you,
my older brother.

00:13:30.010 --> 00:13:32.100
A century later,
we are gathered once again.

00:13:32.390 --> 00:13:35.230
The planets of our solar system
are aligned in a row of twelve!

00:13:35.310 --> 00:13:38.100
The number of months in a year are twelve!

00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:42.860
The number of gods that guard
the universe are twelve!

00:13:43.320 --> 00:13:46.110
The number of guardian angels
guarding Shakyamuni are twelve!

00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:49.030
The number of the apostles
of Christ were twelve!

00:13:49.870 --> 00:13:54.540
And now, the twelve warriors that protect
our beloved country are right here!

00:13:55.330 --> 00:13:59.250
Sea King Ryu from Heilongjiang.
Bailin Temple.

00:14:00.460 --> 00:14:05.050
Sea King Retsu, also from Heilongjiang.
Bailin Temple.

00:14:06.010 --> 00:14:09.220
Sea King Son from Jilin. Sekkendo.

00:14:10.640 --> 00:14:14.060
Sea King Yoh from Shangdong. Kongoken.

00:14:15.520 --> 00:14:18.850
Sea King Chin from Fujian. Sangoken.

00:14:20.270 --> 00:14:23.440
Sea King Jo from Jiangsu. Ryuoken.

00:14:25.030 --> 00:14:28.200
Sea King Moh from Hebei. Jujuken.

00:14:29.910 --> 00:14:32.950
Sea King Samwan from Thailand. Muay Thai.

00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:37.660
Sea King Li from Guangdong. Yakukoken.

00:14:39.160 --> 00:14:43.540
Sea King Han, also from Guangdong. Kenodo.

00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:48.300
Sea King Dorian from America.
Bailin Temple.

00:14:49.680 --> 00:14:53.050
Sea King Jaku from Japan. Kukendo.

00:14:55.350 --> 00:14:59.770
It's tradition that these twelve gather,
but they won't be let off easy.

00:15:00.140 --> 00:15:02.350
We're adding more to this line-up.

00:15:04.190 --> 00:15:08.570
Joining us after 100 years
is the man himself.

00:15:08.900 --> 00:15:13.740
The 146-year-old former
Great Raitai Tournament Champion.

00:15:14.870 --> 00:15:16.160
Please stand, everyone.

00:15:16.540 --> 00:15:17.790
Still going strong,

00:15:17.870 --> 00:15:22.370
please welcome the Sea King
of Sea Kings, Sea Emperor Kaku!

00:15:22.960 --> 00:15:26.880
The ministry has also approved
three last-minute guests.

00:15:28.170 --> 00:15:31.130
Mohammad Alai Jr. from America!

00:15:32.090 --> 00:15:34.180
Yujiro Hanma from Japan!

00:15:35.510 --> 00:15:38.310
Baki Hanma, also from Japan!

00:15:39.220 --> 00:15:42.600
These are your 16 participants
of this Great Raitai Tournament!

00:15:42.690 --> 00:15:45.650
The once-in-a-century, one-day tournament!

00:15:45.730 --> 00:15:48.650
The once-in-a-century chance
to release some major stress

00:15:48.730 --> 00:15:50.400
will now begin!

00:15:52.990 --> 00:15:54.660
Here is the official bracket.

00:15:55.280 --> 00:15:56.280
A bracket?

00:15:56.660 --> 00:15:58.410
But there are only two names.

00:15:58.990 --> 00:16:00.500
Our Sea King Ryu and...

00:16:00.870 --> 00:16:04.170
Yujiro Hanma?

00:16:04.750 --> 00:16:05.920
Who is that?

00:16:06.500 --> 00:16:09.170
We'll see Sea King Ryu,
our God of Battle, in action!

00:16:09.250 --> 00:16:11.170
The victim is a Japanese guy!

00:16:11.840 --> 00:16:15.050
To focus on martial arts
and to ensure fairness,

00:16:15.300 --> 00:16:18.970
we will reveal the names for each match
one at a time.

00:16:19.520 --> 00:16:22.940
If you are not in the next match,
please leave the stage.

00:16:26.480 --> 00:16:27.940
<i>He really showed up.</i>

00:16:28.440 --> 00:16:31.820
<i>He's never fought</i>
<i>in an official tournament before.</i>

00:16:33.150 --> 00:16:34.070
Father...

00:16:34.570 --> 00:16:36.320
Get off the stage already.

00:16:37.120 --> 00:16:38.580
You're breaking the rules.

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:47.080
Now, we have two great men
on the Raitai stage.

00:16:47.380 --> 00:16:50.210
I'd like to bring up an issue here.

00:16:50.710 --> 00:16:51.630
An issue?

00:16:51.880 --> 00:16:52.720
What is it?

00:16:53.510 --> 00:16:57.550
The God of Fists, Sea King Ryu,
is our country's pride.

00:16:58.010 --> 00:17:04.730
But is his opponent, Yujiro Hanma,
worthy of the Raitai stage?

00:17:05.310 --> 00:17:08.900
We at the Ministry of Martial Arts
prepared a suitable test

00:17:09.400 --> 00:17:11.570
for this Japanese martial artist.

00:17:12.780 --> 00:17:16.280
These are common tiles,
a material used on roofs.

00:17:16.610 --> 00:17:18.660
They are extremely durable,

00:17:18.740 --> 00:17:22.790
and were introduced to Japan
from China during the Sui dynasty.

00:17:23.330 --> 00:17:25.710
Since ancient times,
Japanese martial artists

00:17:25.960 --> 00:17:31.500
would measure their true skills by
seeing how many tiles they could break.

00:17:32.090 --> 00:17:37.260
It's said that capable fighters
can easily smash at least ten tiles.

00:17:38.430 --> 00:17:42.260
Here, we have prepared
a staggering 40 tiles.

00:17:42.850 --> 00:17:48.270
We'd like Mr. Hanma to attempt
to break this tower of tiles.

00:17:49.190 --> 00:17:53.110
If you are worthy of standing on
the Raitai stage,

00:17:53.190 --> 00:17:55.940
we would like you to attempt this feat!

00:17:56.400 --> 00:17:59.160
How many tiles can you destroy?

00:17:59.240 --> 00:18:02.200
We would like you to attempt this feat!

00:18:06.460 --> 00:18:07.960
Breaking tiles.

00:18:08.670 --> 00:18:11.040
It's my first time,
now that I think about it.

00:18:13.840 --> 00:18:16.800
These hunks of dirt
are like rice crackers.

00:18:17.130 --> 00:18:21.050
It doesn't show my strength,
no matter how many I break.

00:18:35.190 --> 00:18:36.280
He smashed them all!

00:18:36.740 --> 00:18:39.070
He's a worthy contestant!

00:18:40.780 --> 00:18:41.950
A test?

00:18:42.620 --> 00:18:44.080
What a pointless show.

00:18:44.740 --> 00:18:46.580
Right, Sea King Ryu?

00:18:47.160 --> 00:18:48.580
What do you think?

00:18:49.160 --> 00:18:51.080
These tests don't tell us anything.

00:18:51.790 --> 00:18:54.840
<i>Boards, tiles, concrete blocks,</i>

00:18:54.920 --> 00:18:58.590
<i>bricks, natural stones, bottles,</i>

00:18:59.170 --> 00:19:02.340
<i>ice, paper, fruit...</i>

00:19:03.010 --> 00:19:06.680
These opponents will never talk
nor fight back.

00:19:06.770 --> 00:19:11.850
You can beat, strike, kick, and break
them as much as you want.

00:19:13.190 --> 00:19:15.360
You're taking advantage
of its non-resistance.

00:19:19.820 --> 00:19:20.990
Martial arts

00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:25.870
exist primarily for the weak.

00:19:26.450 --> 00:19:29.080
You're suddenly able to break an object

00:19:29.540 --> 00:19:31.620
that was unbreakable in days past.

00:19:32.080 --> 00:19:36.630
You can actually feel growth
without harming anyone.

00:19:37.420 --> 00:19:40.220
If it's on the path to progress,

00:19:40.970 --> 00:19:43.890
I don't think it's entirely meaningless.

00:19:45.050 --> 00:19:45.890
So?

00:19:49.020 --> 00:19:50.390
I'm going to teach you

00:19:52.350 --> 00:19:56.650
that the growth you felt from those
100 years of painstaking effort

00:19:57.820 --> 00:20:01.150
was just a delusional, insignificant past.

00:20:14.370 --> 00:20:15.380
Don't move.

00:20:16.210 --> 00:20:17.670
Or you'll be sorry.

00:20:19.300 --> 00:20:21.170
Geez, this is what I mean.

00:20:30.020 --> 00:20:31.680
You used him for 100 years.

00:20:32.230 --> 00:20:33.690
Switch him out.

00:20:38.520 --> 00:20:40.940
How could he...

00:20:44.660 --> 00:20:46.700
This is where you announce my win.

00:20:48.200 --> 00:20:49.160
In the meantime,

00:20:50.370 --> 00:20:51.660
I'll leave the stage.

00:20:56.000 --> 00:20:57.790
Yujiro Hanma!

00:20:59.250 --> 00:21:01.800
-It's Retsu!
-Sea King Retsu is here!

00:21:04.630 --> 00:21:06.550
You bastard!

00:21:08.300 --> 00:21:11.060
What's wrong? It's not your turn.

00:21:11.470 --> 00:21:12.980
Fight me!

00:21:13.350 --> 00:21:14.810
Right here, right now!

00:21:18.980 --> 00:21:20.820
Well...

00:21:22.030 --> 00:21:23.820
Now you're talking!

00:21:39.500 --> 00:21:40.340
Master.

00:21:45.260 --> 00:21:46.090
What?

00:21:47.430 --> 00:21:49.180
Are you...

00:21:49.720 --> 00:21:51.100
trying to insult me?

00:21:58.150 --> 00:21:59.980
That was cheap, old man.

00:22:17.370 --> 00:22:19.250
We have a winner!

00:23:42.290 --> 00:23:43.210
IDIOTS FROM PLANET STRONG

00:23:49.170 --> 00:23:51.090
Subtitle translation by Chul Kim
